1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,479
Shortly after his liberation neo initially refuses to accept the truth.
获得自由后不久，Neo 最初拒绝接受真相。

2
00:00:05,479 --> 00:00:11,680
No I don't believe it it's impossible he says after morpheus showed him what the matrix is.
“不，我不信，这不可能，”他在 Morpheus 展示 Matrix 的真相后说道。

3
00:00:11,680 --> 00:00:16,120
He showed a typical reaction of someone confronted with the harsh reality.
作者认为，他表现出人们面对残酷现实时的典型反应。

4
00:00:16,120 --> 00:00:23,840
As the architect of the matrix states in the sequel denial is the most predictable of all human responses.
正如续集里“建筑师”所说，否认是所有人类反应中最可预测的一种。

5
00:00:23,840 --> 00:00:30,000
We can see this when for example we discover that one of our parents isn't our biological parent.
比如发现自己的某一位父母不是亲生父母时，我们能看到这种反应。

6
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:34,280
Or the person we consider our greatest enemy turns out to be our parent.
或者，发现自己认定的最大敌人竟然是自己的父母。

7
00:00:34,280 --> 00:00:42,440
In such cases the truth carries such a magnitude that accepting it shakes one's identity to its very foundations.
在这类情形中，真相影响巨大，接受它会动摇一个人身份认同的根基。

8
00:00:42,440 --> 00:00:46,510
Such a massive shift in perception generally terrifies people.
作者认为，这种对事物看法的巨大改变通常令人恐惧。

9
00:00:46,520 --> 00:00:55,240
Neo asks morpheus I can't go back can I to which morpheus answers but if you could would you really want to.
Neo 问：“我回不去了，对吗？”Morpheus 回答：“就算可以，你真的想回去吗？”

10
00:00:55,240 --> 00:01:04,070
Flatout disregard of the truth is common many people prefer living in a safe bubble of lies to looking outside for the truth.
作者说，彻底无视真相很常见；很多人宁可活在安全的谎言泡泡里，也不愿向外寻找真相。

11
00:01:04,080 --> 00:01:13,110
Living in a cozy false reality can be pretty convenient and comfortable you just have to remain ignorant of everything that could burst your bubble.
活在舒适的虚假现实里可能很方便；只要对会戳破泡泡的东西保持无知即可。

12
00:01:13,120 --> 00:01:20,919
So instead you go along with the deceptive narrative of the herd often amplified by mass media and entertainment.
于是你跟随群体的欺骗性叙事，而大众媒体和娱乐又常把它放大；这是作者的解读。

13
00:01:20,919 --> 00:01:29,280
But we also see the opposite happening like people opposing common knowledge adopting a false truth like the idea that earth is flat.
作者也举出相反情况：有人反对常识，接受错误信念，例如地球是平的。

14
00:01:29,280 --> 00:01:32,960
So truth by and large can be easily fabricated.
因此，作者认为所谓“真相”往往很容易被编造。

15
00:01:32,960 --> 00:01:44,680
Mariam webster provides a definition of truth that goes as follows a judgment proposition or idea that is true or accepted as true.
作者引用词典定义：真相可以是“真实，或被接受为真实的判断、命题或想法”；词典名字幕待核。

16
00:01:44,680 --> 00:01:53,360
Morphe's goal is to liberate the people from the matrix but he also realizes that as long as these people are part of the system they're the enemy.
Morpheus 想把人们从 Matrix 中解放，但他也认为，只要他们仍在系统中，他们就是敌人。

17
00:01:53,360 --> 00:02:03,479
First of all because so called agents protect the matrix these agents function a bit like a security program to keep trojan horses and other malware out.
首先，所谓的探员保护着 Matrix，就像安全程序一样把木马和其他恶意软件挡在外面。

18
00:02:03,479 --> 00:02:07,510
And every human projection is potentially an agent.
每个人类投影都可能成为探员。

19
00:02:07,520 --> 00:02:11,239
Second of all most of them aren't ready to be unplugged.
其次，他们大多数还没准备好被拔掉连接。

20
00:02:11,239 --> 00:02:19,360
Similarly when plato's enlightened man tries to persuade the people in the cave to go outside he meets resistance and ridicule.
类似地，柏拉图寓言中的觉醒者试图说服洞里的人出去，却遭到抵抗和嘲笑。

21
00:02:19,360 --> 00:02:24,640
Plato describes such endeavor as inserting vision into blind eyes.
作者转述柏拉图，把这项努力描述为向盲眼中放入视觉。

22
00:02:24,640 --> 00:02:30,270
It's a waste of time trying to convince someone of the truth if they aren't receptive to it.
作者说，如果对方不愿接受，试图说服他们接受真相就是浪费时间。

23
00:02:30,280 --> 00:02:37,750
Morpheus also states that many are so hopelessly dependent on the system that they'll fight fight to protect it.
Morpheus 也说，许多人如此无助地依赖系统，甚至会为保护它而战。

24
00:02:37,760 --> 00:02:45,630
Similarly socrates asks if these people wouldn't kill the person offering them the truth about their existence.
类似地，苏格拉底问，这些人是否会杀死给他们揭示自身存在真相的人。

25
00:02:45,640 --> 00:02:54,559
Nevertheless plato points to the philosopher's responsibility to act in the interest of the unenlightened ones even if they're hostile.
尽管如此，作者说柏拉图仍强调哲学家有责任为尚未觉醒者的利益行动，即使他们有敌意。

26
00:02:54,559 --> 00:03:02,400
Just as neo morpheus trinity and the other liberated humans do.
就像 Neo、Morpheus、Trinity 和其他得到解放的人所做的那样。

27
00:03:02,400 --> 00:03:13,470
In plato's allegory we see that liberation ultimately positively affects the man who is freed also neo eventually accepts the truth and embraces reality.
在柏拉图寓言里，获得自由最终使那个人受益；Neo 后来也接受真相，拥抱现实。

28
00:03:13,480 --> 00:03:19,559
But what if someone knows the truth but hates it so much that he chooses a false reality.
但如果有人知道真相，却非常厌恶它，以至于选择虚假现实呢？

29
00:03:19,559 --> 00:03:25,799
Here's where a character named cipher comes in cipher admits he regrets taking the red pill.
这时一个叫 Cipher 的人物出现了。他承认，自己后悔吃了红药丸。

30
00:03:25,799 --> 00:03:29,200
Saying to neo almost assuming he feels the same.
他对 Neo 说，仿佛认定对方也有相同感受：

31
00:03:29,200 --> 00:03:36,109
I know what you're thinking cuz right now I'm thinking the same thing actually I've been thinking it ever since I got here.
“我知道你在想什么，因为我现在也在想同样的事。其实从来到这里我就一直在想。”

32
00:03:36,119 --> 00:03:40,780
Why oh why didn't I take the blue pill end quote.
“为什么，为什么当初我没吃蓝药丸？”引文结束。
